Mind, though, that you will destroy your valuable unihorn in case
you stumble across a potion of polymorph. That's trivially solvable
by first dipping something else than your unihorn, but you should
certainly keep that in mind as part of your Standard Procedure for
unID'd dipping.

Contrary to what the other poster says, quaff testing paralysis is
an extremely stupid move; depending on the potions BUC status you
can get killed a dozen times if you take just the above mentioned
duration of the potion effect into consideration. Locking oneself
in a closet and engraving the protecting word as additional safety
means will make it mostly safe, though.

"Picking a just emptied room" is no better or worse than picking an
ordinary empty room, BTW. You should telepthy check, though, whether
the whole level is empty or any monsters sufficiently far away.

No idea why the poster thinks "what people never remember to get".
Speed boots are very apparent. Gauntlets of power as well, but as
opposed to the boots the gauntlets have severe disadvantages as
well, so it depends whether that's a good choice in the first place.
Tinning kit is an interesting tool; an early tool may support you
in getting poison resistance, and later to get some strength - but
only if you're not playing elves. But there are better choices to
choose from that tinning kits.

